<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Dagger</h1>
<p>Average Length: Approx. 6 inches to 1 foot.
Type of Weapon: Very Close Hand-to-hand.
Commonly used by: All classes.
</p><p>These weapons were not widespread in the army, but most of the people in the Middle Ages had one or more. These weapons were small, usually less than a foot long, but generally very sharp. All different designs were used, and they could be either for throwing or hand-to-hand. They were especially popular among merchants and thieves.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla the dagger is a weapon skill of its own, one of the swords (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): one-handed, it slashes, it leans on strength, with some dexterity, and it is quick, as light weapons are. Nearly every guild teaches it: the assassins, conjurers, druids, fighters, knights, necromancers, paladins, sorcerers and thieves from guild level 0, the barbarians from level 2 and the rangers from level 3; many only up to 80% (the necromancers up to 90%). Only the healers don't teach it.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
